            <ArticleTitle>A case of phytodermatitis due to the Ceratocephalus falcatus.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>74-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3109/15569527.2013.788009</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Many people widely use herbal therapies for health problems in the world. Although these herbal therapies sometimes may be useful for some disorders they are not risk free. Ceratocephalus falcatus is an annual, wild plant which is a member of Ranunculaceae family. There are few case reports of phytodermatitis due to the Ranunculaceae family. We present a 58-year-old woman with irritant phytodermatitis due to C. falcatus.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
